# Loan Default Prediction — Home Credit Risk

A machine learning system that predicts whether a loan applicant
will default on their repayment, built on the real-world Home Credit
Default Risk dataset from Kaggle.

## What This Project Does

Most people who need loans have little or no formal credit history.
Banks reject them. Home Credit tries to serve them — but needs a
reliable way to assess repayment risk without traditional credit scores.

This project builds that system. Given a loan application with
demographic and financial information, the model returns a default
probability, a risk level, and a recommendation — approve, review,
or reject.

## The Dataset

- Source: [Home Credit Default Risk — Kaggle](https://www.kaggle.com/competitions/home-credit-default-risk)
- Training rows: 307,511 loan applications
- Features: 122 columns covering income, employment, credit amounts, and external scores
- Default rate: 8.07% — severe class imbalance handled via XGBoost scale_pos_weight

## Key Findings from EDA

- Only 8.07% of applicants defaulted — model evaluation uses AUC-ROC not accuracy
- Younger applicants default at significantly higher rates
- Shorter employment duration strongly correlates with default risk
- EXT_SOURCE_2 and EXT_SOURCE_3 (external credit scores) are the strongest predictors
- The engineered feature CREDIT_INCOME_RATIO ranked highly in feature importance

## Feature Engineering

Six new features were created from existing columns:

- CREDIT_INCOME_RATIO — loan amount relative to annual income
- ANNUITY_INCOME_RATIO — monthly payment burden relative to income
- CREDIT_TERM — estimated loan duration in months
- EXT_SOURCE_MEAN / MIN / MAX — aggregates of three external credit scores
- EMPLOYED_TO_AGE_RATIO — employment stability relative to applicant age

## API

The model is served via FastAPI on port 8004.

```bash
uvicorn api.main:app --reload --port 8004
```

Send a POST request to /predict:

```json
{
  "AMT_CREDIT": 500000,
  "AMT_INCOME_TOTAL": 150000,
  "AMT_ANNUITY": 25000,
  "DAYS_BIRTH": -12000,
  "DAYS_EMPLOYED": -2000,
  "EXT_SOURCE_2": 0.7,
  "EXT_SOURCE_3": 0.65
}
```

Response:

```json
{
  "default_probability": 0.0821,
  "risk_level": "LOW",
  "recommendation": "APPROVE"
}
```

## How to Run

```bash
git clone https://github.com/yourusername/loan-default-prediction.git
cd loan-default-prediction
python -m venv venv
venv\Scripts\activate
pip install -r requirements.txt
jupyter notebook notebooks/loan_default_prediction.ipynb
```

Run all cells top to bottom. Then start the API:

```bash
uvicorn api.main:app --reload --port 8004
```

## A Note on the Bug I Fixed

During preprocessing, a column called DAYS_EMPLOYED_CLEAN was
accidentally created during EDA for the training set but never
applied to the test set. This caused a feature mismatch error
when the imputer tried to transform the test data.

Fix: dropped DAYS_EMPLOYED_CLEAN before imputation since
YEARS_EMPLOYED already captured the same information cleanly.
Lesson: any transformation applied to train must be applied to
test at the same step.

